 "readme": "# Nepal Economic Distress Early Warning System\n\nThis project is an explainable machine learning dashboard for monitoring and predicting economic distress risk in Nepal. It combines a Flask web app, interactive UI components, and SHAP-based feature explanations to help users explore macroeconomic scenarios and understand model predictions.\n\n## Features\n\n- Interactive scenario inputs for macroeconomic variables\n- Real-time distress probability prediction\n- Color-coded result card with risk status\n- SHAP-based feature contribution visualization\n- Prediction history for comparing previous runs\n- Full dashboard view for macroeconomic analysis\n\n## Project Structure\n\n- `app.py` - Flask app and prediction API\n- `templates/` - HTML templates for the main UI\n- `static/` - CSS and JavaScript assets\n- `dashboard/` - standalone dashboard page\n- `data/` - model and dataset files\n\n## Run Locally\n\n1. Open the project folder\n2. Install dependencies if needed\n3. Start the app:\n\n```bash\npython app.py\n```\n\n4. Open the browser at:\n\n- Main app: http://127.0.0.1:5000\n- Dashboard: http://127.0.0.1:5000/dashboard\n\n## Notes\n\nThis project uses a trained machine learning model and SHAP explainability for interpreting predictions.\n",
